  "findings": [
    "Issue 100 already supplied revision-checked signatures and source summaries. The remaining submission callers still used uncached effectiveComparisonSettings.",
    "Without finding focus, effectiveComparisonSettings sorted membership IDs and counted both sides for every scene submission and selection-helper submission.",
    "With finding focus, effectiveComparisonSettings rehashed the geometry hierarchy in both stages. The final focus draw separately rehashed it again.",
    "Existing surface and diagnostic GPU buffers were already reused. The measured repeated CPU work was input resolution, not GPU geometry rebuilding."
  ],
  "fix": [
    "Resolve display mode from current runtime input counts and signature, while continuing to read live settings, focus, detector state and per-stage GPU result revisions.",
    "Supply the same current signature to diagnostic and UV finding-focus validation.",
    "Skip disabled analyses before resolving submission inputs. Remove a duplicate stale-result check already guaranteed by comparisonStagesReady.",
    "Retain uncached resolution when the runtime snapshot is absent or stale."
  ],
